{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>See all the signs</b> etc. The sages said: of the three signs written above, we find that only one was performed before Pharaoh — ״יהי לתנין.״" "<b>And I will strengthen his heart.</b> One should not say that HaShem holds and hardens hearts so as not to return to Him if they wish to return. Rather, this is what it says: I will strengthen his heart so that he does not die from terror, and his heart does not grow faint from fear, until all the plagues are completed. So too you shall interpret ״ואני אקשה את לב פרעה״ (and I will harden Pharaoh's heart). A proof for this: ״כי אתה שלחתי את ידי ואך אותך״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:08.644396938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}